02:01:41.930 --> 02:01:43.670
I'm a PI, as you said.

02:01:43.670 --> 02:01:46.790
I used to be a graduate student
and a post-doc trainee myself,

02:01:46.790 --> 02:01:50.300
doing all of this on the ground
hands on experimentation.

02:01:50.300 --> 02:01:51.797
It's so hard to do.

02:01:51.797 --> 02:01:52.880
It's so hard to do, right?

02:01:52.880 --> 02:01:54.630
It's so hard to think
through all of that.

02:01:54.630 --> 02:01:57.140
Now, I'm a PI, I get
to be an idea person

02:01:57.140 --> 02:01:59.090
and just say, hey,
why don't you do this

02:01:59.090 --> 02:02:01.160
and hey, what do you
think about that.

02:02:01.160 --> 02:02:03.680
And they, of course,
intellectually

02:02:03.680 --> 02:02:08.330
contributes so much to
these planned experiments.

02:02:08.330 --> 02:02:10.530
But they also do the
really hard work.

02:02:10.530 --> 02:02:14.245
And so I just want to say
thank you graduate students.

02:02:14.245 --> 02:02:15.620
Thank you to my
graduate students

02:02:15.620 --> 02:02:17.000
and all graduate
students out there.

02:02:17.000 --> 02:02:17.690
Thank you post-docs.

02:02:17.690 --> 02:02:18.898
ANDREW HUBERMAN: --underpaid.

02:02:18.898 --> 02:02:22.280
And listen, and to the major
